        "original_id": "951858fb-57a6-5471-a0ed-e45fb5c92519",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacky Ickx, Pedro Rodríguez\n- Organizations: BRM, Ferrari\n- Events: 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, 1979 Can-Am season, 24 Hours of Le Mans, Dakar Rally\n- Topics: Formula One, Can-Am Championship\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Pedro Rodríguez finished second for the BRM team.\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Ferrari driver Jacky Ickx finished third.\n- Jacky Ickx was born on 1 January 1945 in Brussels and is a Belgian former racing driver.\n- Jacky Ickx achieved eight Formula One wins and 25 Formula One podium finishes.\n- Jacky Ickx won the 24 Hours of Le Mans six times.\n- In the 1979 Can-Am season, Jacky Ickx was declared champion.\n- In the 1979 Can-Am season, Jacky Ickx won five of the ten rounds and finished second at Road Atlanta.\n- Jacky Ickx also won the Can-Am Championship in 1979 and was a former winner of the Dakar Rally.",
